# Helgrind suppressions for the vortex scenario harness.
# Helgrind models happens-before via pthread primitives and does NOT understand
# C11 atomics/fences, which vortex uses for cross-thread signaling (shutdown
# flags, generation counters, connection pin counts). Those show up as false
# races here; suppress the confirmed-benign atomic sites, not real bugs.
#
# Matched narrowly by call site (atomic op + its immediate vortex caller) so a
# real race in other code is never masked. The mangled tuple type in the loop
# thread's frames is intentionally left to the `...` wildcard: it changes with
# the thread-arg layout and is not what we are keying on.

# The per-loop shutdown flag: main thread stores `true` (requestShutdown) while
# each loop thread relaxed-loads it in its run loop. An Atomic[bool] is correct
# lock-free signaling; helgrind just cannot see the C11 ordering.
{
   vortex-shutdown-flag-store
   Helgrind:Race
   fun:_ZN7atomics5store*
   fun:_ZN6server15requestShutdown*
   ...
}
{
   vortex-shutdown-flag-load
   Helgrind:Race
   fun:_ZN7atomics4load*
   fun:_ZN9eventloop3run*
   ...
}
